card.statement:
Let $T(L)=T(l_{ij})$ be a f\/ixed tableau of height $n$.

- sep=0pt

- [(i)] $\mathcal{B}(T(L)):=\big\{T(L+z): z\in \mathbb{Z}^{\frac{n(n-1)}{2}}\big\}$.

- [(ii)] $V(T(L)):= \Span \mathcal{B}(T(L))$.

- [(iii)] For any $T(R)=T(r_{ij})\in \mathcal{B}(T(L))$ and for any $1<p\leq n$, $1\leq s\leq p$ and $1\leq u\leq
p-1$ we def\/ine:

- sep=0pt

- [(a)] $\omega_{p,s,u}(T(R)):=r_{p,s}-r_{p-1,u}$;

- [(b)] $\Omega(T(R)):=\{(p,s,u): \omega_{p,s,u}(T(R))\in \mathbb{Z}\}$;

- [(c)] $\Omega^{+}(T(R)):=\{(p,s,u): \omega_{p,s,u}(T(R))\in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}\}$;

- [(d)] $\mathcal{N}(T(R)):=\{T(Q)\in \mathcal{B}(T(L)): \Omega^{+}(T(R))\subseteq \Omega^{+}(T(Q))\}$;

- [(e)] $ W(T(R)):=\Span \mathcal{N}(T(R))$;

- [(f)] $U\cdot T(R)$: the $\mathfrak{gl}(n)$-submodule of $V(T(L))$ generated by $T(R)$.
